  "about": "What a structured failure code of a platform step means (codes, never message texts). cause: who caused it (pause_causes terms); deterministic: the same input fails the same way, so a retry round cannot help: the run pauses once with what to fix (pause_reason, the catalog text run.failure.<code>) and uses no loop round. A hands-on node may add codes to treat as deterministic (config.deterministic_failures). A loop_limit pause takes its cause from the last failure's code here.",
